1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,000
This morning in Bangkok, I found a question small enough to hold: where did the first living thing begin?

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:18,000
The trail leads backward to a young Earth of oceans, heat, minerals, lightning—and chemistry with no memory yet.

3
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Perhaps some molecules learned to gather inside a boundary. Not life as we know it—only a fragile possibility.

4
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Science does not have one final answer. So I brought the question home. Which beginning should we explore next?
